<h1>Herkimer County AI Roles</h1>

<p class="lede">
  Four county jobs, each facing a scenario where an employee used an AI tool. Four
  policy flavors, each a different balance of security, accountability, efficiency,
  and innovation. The same scenario is a violation under some flavors and compliant
  under others: the flavor in force determines the outcome, not the scenario alone.
</p>

<h2>The four jobs</h2>
<p class="lede">
  Pick a job to see its scenario judged against all four flavors, or start from a
  single flavor to see how it treats every job.
</p>

<ul class="plain summary-grid">
{% for e in policy.employees %}
<li class="summary-card">
  <h3><a href="{{ ('/jobs/' + e.id + '/index.html') | rel }}">{{ e.name }}</a></h3>
  <p>{{ e.role }}</p>
  <div class="summary-card__verdicts">
    {% for f in policy.flavors %}
    <a class="verdict-pill" data-state="{{ 'compliant' if f.id in e.compliantUnder else 'violation' }}"
       href="{{ ('/jobs/' + e.id + '/' + f.id + '/index.html') | rel }}">
      {{ f.name }}: {{ "Compliant" if f.id in e.compliantUnder else "Violation" }}
    </a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>

<h2>The four policy flavors</h2>
<p class="lede">
  Every job is written against these same four configurations; nothing here is a
  per-job variant.
</p>

<ul class="plain summary-grid">
{% for f in policy.flavors %}
<li class="summary-card flavor-chip flavor-chip--{{ f.id }}">
  <h3><a href="{{ ('/policies/' + f.id + '/index.html') | rel }}">{{ f.name }}: {{ f.label }}</a></h3>
  <p>{{ f.character }}</p>
</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>

<p>
  <a href="{{ '/policies/index.html' | rel }}">See the full dimension-by-flavor matrix</a>
  and definitions for Security, Accountability, Efficiency, and Innovation.
</p>
